Specific signs of passive-aggressive behavior include:

- resentment and opposition to the demands of others – especially of those in authority;

- resistance to cooperation, procrastination,

- intentional mistakes in response to the demands of others;

- a cynical, sullen, or hostile attitude;

- frequent complaints about feeling underappreciated or cheated.

